id: pm-vcs-4ff1
title: Cross-tenant denial without existence leakage
description: "Every object and ref read, write, copy, list and update across tenants must be denied without leaking whether the object exists. Spec only — tracked as an open child for a future pass."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-28T13:43:14.362Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-05T07:00:49.864Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: pi-agent
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-5h6j,parent,"2026-08-28T15:22:42.163Z",claude,"cli:update:dep",detected
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T20:11:19.300Z",pi-agent,"PR #48 review confirmed this acceptance criterion is intentionally not implemented. The branch contains no cross-tenant authorization implementation or passing acceptance evidence for this child, so it remains open with its written specification."
  "2026-09-12T23:35:50.373Z",pi-agent,"Audit 2026-09-13: EXISTS — nothing. The description says spec only. grep for tenant/Tenant in engine/ returns no matches. No cross-tenant code exists. REMAINS — the full feature: every object and ref operation across tenants denied without leaking object existence."
  "2026-10-05T06:14:07.335Z",pi-glm,"Design: authorization is checked before any repository byte is touched, and every failure that happens before it succeeds - unknown token, absent token scope, missing repository, traversal-shaped repository name, wrong tenant - produces the same status, content-type and body bytes, so a caller cannot distinguish refusal reasons. A read-scoped token hitting a write endpoint on a repository it may read gets a distinct 403, because that caller can already prove the repository exists by advertising it. Adversarial tests will diff the raw responses across all refusal causes."
  "2026-10-05T06:49:32.608Z",codex-sol,"Hardened authorization boundaries after inspecting the interrupted implementation: scoped but absent repositories now receive the fixed denial, including write requests; symlink repository/control aliases and linked instances are refused; denial responses omit Date and close the connection so complete response bytes can be compared. Added object-query and bundled-push count limits, positive limit validation, and token-free client error URLs."
  "2026-10-05T07:00:49.864Z",codex-sol,"Adversarial denial now compares complete raw HTTP responses over TCP across absent/bad tokens, wrong tenants, scoped missing repositories, traversal spellings and every transport endpoint. Raw TCP preserves hostile request-target bytes in Node and Bun. Readable read-only tokens receive the explicit write refusal. Focused HTTP source coverage is 100/100/100/100 and native Bun tests pass. Separate follow-up pm-vcs-00mb records the existing unreadable-config fallback outside this authorization change."
